== AS-IS

+ Fixing the prose in eleven filed tasks so `just docs::vale-tasks` passes.
+ 🔴 `word_count` counts every token in a section, fenced code included, and a project cannot change that without a Rust change:

```
$ mt check
error: truth/tasks/2026-11/give-the-templates-their-own-command.typ:33: body.content.rules.cap-as-is-at-120-words: cut this section to under 120 words, or split the task in two
note: section `AS-IS` must contain at most 120 words (found 126)
```

The same section splits 116 words total, 89 of them the fenced listing and 27 the prose.

+ `min-words` and `max-words` are two keys for one bound, and neither carries a unit.

== TO-BE

- 🟢 `assert = { words = { max = 120, count = "prose" } }` replaces `max-words`, and `words = { min = 10, max = 120 }` replaces both keys.
- 🟢 `count` is `all` (the default), `prose` or `text`.
- 🟢 `[tasks.body.content] words = { count = "prose" }` sets the unit once for every inherited rule.
- 🟢 `mt` refuses a `words` assert that carries neither `min` nor `max`.
- 🟢 `mt` refuses a section default that carries `min` or `max`, and a bound stays visible on the rule.

```
$ mt check
note: section `AS-IS` must contain at most 120 words (found 27)
```

== Changes

- `crates/mindtape/src/body/content.rs`: `ContentAssert::Words(WordSpec)` replaces `MinWords` and `MaxWords`. `WordSpec` holds `min`, `max` and `count`. `WordCount` is the `all|prose|text` enum with a `Deserialize` impl like `DensityUnit`'s. `ContentConfig` gains `words: WordDefaults`.
- `crates/mindtape/src/body/content_gate/mod.rs`: `word_count` takes the unit, and `strip_fenced_code` and `mask_inline_code` become `pub(super)`.
- `crates/mindtape/src/body/content_gate/content_gate_density.rs`: the two helpers lose their private visibility.
- `crates/mindtape/src/config/schema.rs`: the `words` table and the section key.
- `crates/mindtape/src/packs/tasks.toml`, `crates/mindtape/src/packs/dogfood.toml`: the four caps move to `words = { max = N }`.
- `.mindtape/config.toml`: `[tasks.body.content] words = { count = "prose" }`.
- `schema/config.schema.json`: regenerated by `mt schema --write`.
- `www/content/rules.typ`: the `words` table, the three units, and the section default.
- `CHANGELOG.md`: an entry under `[Unreleased]` `Changed`.

== Out of scope

- The cap values. They stay as they are.
- `must-match` and `must-not-match`. A regex over the raw slice still sees code, which is what a shape rule needs.
- A `density` section default. Its `per` stays on the rule.

== Dogfood

This repo writes `[tasks.body.content] words = { count = "prose" }`, so all four inherited caps count prose and none of them changes its bound. The eleven tasks filed in 2026-11 stop spending their AS-IS budget on the output they quote.
